        "original_id": "fb8661c2-4177-54a6-85e5-1ee1946c820d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ottokar Kernstock, Joseph Haydn\n- Works: Sei gesegnet ohne Ende, Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser, Deutschlandlied\n- Places: Germany\n- Topics: national anthem, Classical period, chamber music\n\nFacts:\n- Joseph Haydn was born on 31 March 1732 and died on 31 May 1809.\n- Joseph Haydn was an Austrian composer of the Classical period.\n- Joseph Haydn was instrumental in the development of chamber music such as the piano trio.\n- Joseph Haydn's contributions to musical form earned him the epithets \"Father of the Symphony\" and \"Father of the String Quartet\".\n- Ottokar Kernstock wrote \"Sei gesegnet ohne Ende\".\n- \"Sei gesegnet ohne Ende\" was sung to the tune of Joseph Haydn's \"Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser\".\n- The tune of \"Gott erhalte Franz den Kaiser\" is also used for the \"Deutschlandlied\".\n- Since 1922, the \"Deutschlandlied\" has been the national anthem of Germany.",
